      "raw_mention": "$MDA",
      "text": "Space stocks are the easiest 100x I've ever seen.\n\nBut I'm noticing space bulls are making a deadly mistake: obsessing over price action. We're no longer in a future forward thinking market. The easy money on space is over now, but that's your advantage. \n\nMy view? These stocks should be nowhere but a retirement account separate from your individual that you never trade.\n\nIf you're playing the 2050-2070 game, we're talking disgusting wealth with these stocks. For every business on earth there will be one in space, and the market is far too large for only $SPCX to win.\n\nWhat is more asymmetrical than this thesis of owning the next economy past earth? Every important company building in this market is now public. You can own ALL of them. Some may fail but the few that win, win huge.\n\n$ASTS $FLY $RKLB $PL $LUNR $MDA $SPCX",
